.SH AUTH ON ACTION HOOKS
An auth on action policy can ask for a login again before these actions.
See
.B Auth On Action Policy
in
.BR otpme\-policy (1).
An aclgroup has the hooks every object type has, and these:
.RS
.PP
.na
.nh
add_aclgroup, add_entry, remove_aclgroup, remove_entry.
.hy
.ad
.RE
.\" END AUTH ON ACTION HOOKS
.SH FILES
.na
.nh
.TP
\fI/var/lib/otpme/tree/\fR
The objects of the realm.
An ACL group is the directory \fI<name>.aclgroup\fR in the directory of its unit, e.g. \fI<realm>.realm/<site>.site/aclgroups.unit/USERMANAGER.aclgroup/\fR, with its settings in \fIobject.json\fR, on the nodes of every site, never on a host.
Change them with the commands above, not in the files.
.hy
